<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Empires of the Steppe</h1><p class="ws-lede">How mounted nomads built some of the largest states in history, from the Xiongnu to Timur.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/steppe-empires">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Genghis Khan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Chagatai Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Khazar Khaganate</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Xiongnu Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mongol Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Gokturk Empire</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Xiongnu Empire</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;The first great steppe empire of eastern Eurasia, united by Modu Chanyu around 209 BCE, forced Han China into decades of appeasement.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 5, <b>Genghis Khan</b>: &#8220;Temüjin unified the rival Mongol and Turkic tribes and was proclaimed Genghis Khan at a kurultai in 1206.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 9, <b>Timur</b>: &#8220;Rising within the Chagatai Khanate, Timur used the Mongol framework of legitimacy to build an empire from Anatolia to the borders of China.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;How mounted nomads built some of the largest states in history, from the Xiongnu to Timur.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/steppe-empires. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Empires of the Steppe</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Xiongnu Empire <span>from 318 BCE</span></li><li>Gokturk Empire <span>from 546 CE</span></li><li>Khazar Khaganate <span>from 650 CE</span></li><li>Genghis Khan <span>born c. 1162 CE</span></li><li>Mongol Empire <span>from 1206 CE</span></li><li>Chagatai Empire <span>from 1225 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
